    <releases>
      <release type="stable" version="1.7.2" timestamp="1789603200">
        <description>
          <p>Your writing is kept safer, and the interlinears show more.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>A daily copy of your notes, journal and sermons is kept on this device. Restore keeps a copy of what it replaces.</li>
            <li>Closing the app or logging out no longer loses the last sentence you typed.</li>
            <li>Opening the app a second time no longer risks your notes. It brings the open window forward.</li>
            <li>Find and replace in journal entries and sermons, with Ctrl+F.</li>
            <li>The Greek interlinear can show the words other editions add or change.</li>
            <li>The Hebrew interlinear can show the form the scribes wrote under the form that is read.</li>
            <li>Type a verse reference in the GNOME search to see it and open it.</li>
            <li>Ctrl+D bookmarks the chapter. Alt+[ and Alt+] go back and forward.</li>
            <li>The annotations list shows the verse and updates itself.</li>
            <li>Highlights sat one word late when footnotes were hidden. This is fixed.</li>
          </ul>
        </description>
      </release>
      <release type="stable" version="1.7.1" timestamp="1789430400">
        <description>
          <p>Fixes for writing sermons.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Giving a sermon a series could close the app. This is fixed.</li>
            <li>Typing in a long sermon no longer gets slower as the text grows.</li>
            <li>Russian: the verse menu item for a new journal entry no longer reads as “add a bookmark”.</li>
          </ul>
        </description>
      </release>
      <release type="stable" version="1.7.0" timestamp="1789344000">
        <description>
          <p>A place to write: a journal, sermons, and a new Today page.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>A journal. Write an entry about one passage, several, or none, and add or remove passages later.</li>
            <li>Sermons. Keep each sermon with its passages, its main idea, its series and the days you preached it. Print or export it on its own.</li>
            <li>While you write a sermon, bring in your notes, highlights, verses, cross-references and word studies on the passage.</li>
            <li>The Annotations window has three pages: Annotations, Journal and Sermons, each with its own search and filters.</li>
            <li>Room to write, with buttons for bold, italic, headings, quotes and lists, and a word count.</li>
            <li>Print, export and compare translations from the new ⋮ button, or with Ctrl+P, Ctrl+E and Ctrl+Shift+C. Before, they were only in the right-click menu.</li>
            <li>The Today page shows the first verse of the day&apos;s reading, on a new parchment background.</li>
            <li>Search finds your own notes and entries as well as Bible verses.</li>
            <li>The right-click menu is shorter and grouped.</li>
            <li>Fixed: double-clicking a word said “No entry” even with dictionaries installed, and a reading plan could say it was done when it was not.</li>
          </ul>
        </description>
      </release>
      <release type="stable" version="1.6.2" timestamp="1788998400">
        <description>
          <p>Your marks now show in every translation, and many fixes.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Highlights, underlines, notes and tags now show in every translation, not only the one you made them in. The Study Journal is now called Annotations.</li>
            <li>Export, print and copy work for Bibles from eBible, and marks made in them land on the right verse.</li>
            <li>Psalm numbers are right in the Clementine Vulgate and the Russian Synodal Bible from eBible.</li>
            <li>“Match case” no longer turns an OR search into an AND search.</li>
            <li>A link to a book your Bible does not have now tells you which book is missing, instead of doing nothing.</li>
            <li>The Orthodox Old Calendar is offered beside the New Calendar.</li>
            <li>Russian readers get the Orthodox troparion in Church Slavonic, not in English.</li>
            <li>Dates show in the app&apos;s language, not always in English.</li>
            <li>A stray space before commas is gone from the Today page, devotionals, cross-references, dictionaries and collects.</li>
            <li>Highlights cover the whole verse and stay beside the right text.</li>
          </ul>
        </description>
      </release>
    </releases>
